        "For three weeks before the Mid-Autumn Festival, Mr Liang made paper lanterns in a workshop in a lane in Yuexiu. This year the neighbourhood committee ordered six hundred lanterns, twice the usual number, because two more streets had joined the celebration and wanted the same kind.",
        "The order arrived in mid-August, later than usual. Mr Liang and his two helpers cut bamboo strips in the morning and glued red paper at night. A simple lantern took about twenty minutes. Six hundred lanterns meant two hundred hours of work, and they had nineteen days.",
